# Zorya Classifier (project pointer)

Canonical shared rules live under `/root/.cursor/rules/` (repository cleanliness, Context7 usage, Luna prose authorship, Cursor-limit fallback, and other owner-wide policies). Do not duplicate or contradict them here. Persistent/user-facing prose is authored by `gpt-6-luna` with high reasoning and `fork_turns=none` under `/root/.cursor/rules/text-authorship.mdc`; this is the normal narrow prose exception and does not authorize changes to executable logic, tests, or runtime configuration. The separate technical fallback in `/root/.cursor/rules/cursor-limit-fallback.mdc` authorizes Luna to continue an already authorized technical task after structured `resource_exhausted` or a recognizable `ActionRequiredError` containing the exact string `You're out of usage` (whitespace normalization is defined by that canonical rule). A generic `ActionRequiredError` without that string does not qualify. That rule requires stopping Cursor without further probes and does not change the human-selected main model.

Project contract and contributor invariants: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

Russian guides: [docs/architecture.ru.md](../../docs/architecture.ru.md), [docs/development.ru.md](../../docs/development.ru.md). Refactor waves and Composer workflow: [docs/refactoring-plan.ru.md](../../docs/refactoring-plan.ru.md), [docs/agents.ru.md](../../docs/agents.ru.md).

Offline test catalog: default `npm test` → `node --import tsx scripts/run-classified-tests.mjs portable` (Zod `scripts/test-catalog.ts`); `local-evidence` has five files and 16 cases (H5 mock replay, grounded-mask mock replay, H10 minimal frozen manifest, Jev native-box local evidence, and four H8 zero-query checks against the pinned external protocol/predecessor root `UI_STATE_DEV40_ROOT`). The four H8 checks require real frozen evidence; the similarly named portable test uses a synthetic fixture and does not substitute for those receipts. Optional native H6/H8 checks remain in `portable`. `npm run test:local-evidence`, `npm run test:python-native`; standalone MCP tests use `npm run test:mcp` and its package-cwd runner. Agent workflow: human-selected main orchestrator plans/shows waves and integrates; every Codex subagent `gpt-6-luna`/high/`fork_turns=none`; coordinator owns Cursor CLI and dispatches only `composer-2.5-fast`; Composer executor edits itself and must not recursively launch Cursor CLI. Russian roles and plan visibility: [docs/agents.ru.md](../../docs/agents.ru.md). Owner-wide rules: `/root/.cursor/rules/` (main orchestrator and every spawned Codex subagent read `context7.mdc`, `repository-cleanliness.mdc`, `text-authorship.mdc`, and `cursor-limit-fallback.mdc`; coordinator includes applicable constraints in Composer prompts).
